; Ozbound level data: Bluebrook, the vertical-slice world (meadow, village, forest).
;
; Same format as assets/maps/meadow.map, plus optional sections for the village slice.
; Lines starting with ';' are comments. Blank lines are ignored. Sections may appear in any
; order, each at most once. Required: [map], [player]. [guide] makes this a story level; a
; level without one is a region (scenery only, see yellow_road_east.map).
; Optional: [guide], [moonpetals], [nodes], [signs], [npcs], [places], [creatures], [houses],
; [plots], [exits].
;
; Coordinates are "x y" in tiles. x counts right from the left edge; y counts UP from the
; BOTTOM row of [map] (the last row listed is y = 0).
;
; [npcs]      id x y appearance Display name    (the guide is NOT listed here; id `guide` is reserved)
;             appearances: traveller, guide, apothecary, woodcutter, ferrywoman, surveyor
; [places]    id x y Display name               (targets for `visit <id>` quest objectives)
; [creatures] id x y                            (ids come from assets/bestiary/*.bestiary)
; [houses]    id x y width height door_side Name (door_side: north, south, east, west; x y is the
;             south-west corner; walls, doorway and floor are stamped over open grass or path)
; [plots]     id x y width height Name           (a plot holds whole houses and a garden or vineyard)
; [exits]     x y LOCATION_ID arrive_x arrive_y Label   (stepping on x y travels to that region)
;
; Geography: a meadow in the south-west, a river at x = 20-21 crossed by the wooden bridge
; on the main road (y = 9), the village of Bluebrook east of the river (three plots, each with
; a house and a garden or vineyard), and a forest along the north edge. The road leaves the
; map at its east end (x = 38, y = 9) for the Yellow Brick Road.

[map]
; '.' grass, '=' path, '~' water, 'T' tree, '#' rock, 'F' fence, 'S' signpost,
; 'g' garden bed, 'v' vineyard row (both block movement; walk the grass lanes between).
; Houses are not drawn here: the [houses] section stamps walls, a doorway, and floor.
